--TEST--
A comparison whose two sides share no value is refused at the comparison itself, and its help names what to write instead — a cast for two scalars, `as int` for an enum against a number, and no cast where no conversion joins the two — while `<` names `Core\Str::compare` for text and `Comparable` for an object, `rule:expressions/disjoint-comparison-refused`, `rule:classes/comparable`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:expressions/comparison-and-equality
// Two sides that share no value are refused where they are written, and the
// help names what to write instead — a cast for most rows, `as int` for an
// enum against a number, and no cast at all where no conversion joins the
// two. Ordering takes numbers, two `bool`s and two objects of one
// `Comparable` class; every other operand is refused the same way.
enum Rank { Bronze, Silver }
enum Suit { Clubs, Hearts }

class Meter { public function constructor(public int $reading) {} }
class Gauge { public function constructor(public int $reading) {} }

int $n = 1;
string $s = "1";
bytes $b = "1" as bytes;
Meter $meter = new Meter(1);
Gauge $gauge = new Gauge(1);
array<int> $xs = [1];

var $numberAgainstText = $n == $s;
var $textAgainstBytes = $s == $b;
var $enumAgainstInt = Rank::Bronze == 0;
var $twoEnums = Rank::Bronze == Suit::Clubs;
var $presentAgainstNull = $n == null;
var $twoClasses = $meter == $gauge;
var $twoStrings = $s < $s;
var $twoBytes = $b < $b;
var $twoArrays = $xs < $xs;
var $twoObjects = $meter < $meter;
echo "unreached\n";
// covers: lang:enums/comparing-cases
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0466]: `int` and `string` are disjoint; no value is both, so this comparison is always false
   --> %s:21:26
   |
21 | var $numberAgainstText = $n == $s;
   |                          ^^^^^^^^ compared here
   = help: convert one side deliberately and then compare — `$s == ($n as string)`

error[E0466]: `string` and `bytes` are disjoint; no value is both, so this comparison is always false
   --> %s:22:25
   |
22 | var $textAgainstBytes = $s == $b;
   |                         ^^^^^^^^ compared here
   = help: convert one side deliberately and then compare — `$s == ($n as string)`

error[E0466]: `Rank` and `int` are disjoint; no value is both, so this comparison is always false
   --> %s:23:23
   |
23 | var $enumAgainstInt = Rank::Bronze == 0;
   |                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ compared here
   = help: an enum case carries an integer — compare `$e as int` against the number

error[E0466]: `Rank` and `Suit` are disjoint; no value is both, so this comparison is always false
   --> %s:24:17
   |
24 | var $twoEnums = Rank::Bronze == Suit::Clubs;
   |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ compared here
   = help: an enum case is only ever equal to a case of the same enum — `match` on it, or compare `$e as int` on both sides

error[E0466]: `int` cannot hold `null`, so this test is always false
   --> %s:25:27
   |
25 | var $presentAgainstNull = $n == null;
   |                           ^^^^^^^^^^ compared here
   = help: declare the binding nullable — `?T` — if it is meant to be optional, or drop the test

error[E0466]: `Meter` and `Gauge` are disjoint; no value is both, so this comparison is always false
   --> %s:26:19
   |
26 | var $twoClasses = $meter == $gauge;
   |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ compared here
   = help: two unrelated classes have no value in common — compare something both of them carry, such as an id property

error[E0715]: `<` has no meaning for `string`
   --> %s:27:19
   |
27 | var $twoStrings = $s < $s;
   |                   ^^^^^^^ ordered here
   = help: `Core\Str::compare` is the ordering two strings have; `rule:types/arithmetic` tabulates no `<` for text, because PHP's own answer there is a conversion Novis never makes by itself

error[E0715]: `<` has no meaning for `bytes`
   --> %s:28:17
   |
28 | var $twoBytes = $b < $b;
   |                 ^^^^^^^ ordered here
   = help: `rule:types/arithmetic`'s `< <= > >= <=>` row is the numeric types, plus two objects of one `Comparable` class (`rule:classes/comparable`); this operand is on neither half

error[E0715]: `<` has no meaning for `array<int>`
   --> %s:29:18
   |
29 | var $twoArrays = $xs < $xs;
   |                  ^^^^^^^^^ ordered here
   = help: `rule:types/arithmetic`'s `< <= > >= <=>` row is the numeric types, plus two objects of one `Comparable` class (`rule:classes/comparable`); this operand is on neither half

error[E0411]: `Meter` does not implement `Comparable`; ordering two objects with `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=`/`<=>` requires it
   --> %s:30:19
   |
30 | var $twoObjects = $meter < $meter;
   |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ compared here
   = help: implement `Comparable`'s `compareTo(self $other): int` on the class

error: aborting due to 10 errors
